## Complete Feature List
The modern @icp-sdk ecosystem consists of modular layers covering all essential dApp features: [2] 

   1. @icp-sdk/core/agent: The foundational layer used to initialize an HttpAgent to handle secure data transfers via query (read-only) and update (state-changing) calls to any smart contract (canister).
   2. @icp-sdk/core/identity: Cryptographic identity tools (like Ed25519KeyIdentity) used to sign queries and updates.
   3. @icp-sdk/core/candid: The data serialization tool (IDL) used to encode arguments and decode returns dynamically when communicating with canisters.
   4. @icp-sdk/core/principal: A parser for identifiers to explicitly reference text-based user accounts and canister locations.
   5. @icp-sdk/auth: Seamless browser authentication connecting directly to Internet Identity to obtain verifiable user delegation certificates.
   6. @icp-sdk/signer: Orchestration logic allowing apps to securely offload execution signing requests to non-custodial asset wallets (like OISY or NFID). [1, 2, 3] 

